[{"id":2983649861,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6x1uJF","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. This is a great start :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_pr_108219.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21040506/test_pr_108219.zip)\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- Area width and height should use a single `area` Vector2 property instead of two separate float properties. While doing so, make sure to use `PROPERTY_HINT_LINK` for the property so you can adjust the width proportionally to the current height (and vice versa). You can clamp the value to positive numbers in the `set_area()` setter (this ensures it also affects script-based usage).\r\n- Gizmo behavior and icons look good to me.\r\n- I've only tested this in Forward+, as Mobile will print a lot of errors and not render anything. On Compatibility, area lights are not supported but rendering works correctly otherwise.\r\n  - There should be a node configuration warning on AreaLight3D when in Compatibility, similar to the Decal node's existing node configuration warning.\r\n- Like with lights that use a dual paraboloid shadow mode, meshes need to be subdivided enough (relative to the size of the area light) for shadows to look correct:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb14853e-f00f-4825-a93d-ac91255f6c8f\r\n\r\nThis is most noticeable on shadows with a low blur value:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5e96398-6670-4a4c-b902-cad1f45dfe6a\r\n\r\n- Light/shadow distance fade works correctly.\r\n- Volumetric fog doesn't take area lights into account yet.\r\n- **Hard** positional shadow quality looks the same as **Soft Very Low**. Ideally, **Hard** should disable shadow blurring entirely like it does with other light types to maximize performance on low-end GPUs.\r\n- **High** and **Ultra** soft shadow qualities can be very expensive with lights that have a high blur value (even `1.0` is quite blurry out of the box), so beware. Consider using TAA or FSR2 to get temporal smoothing (and keep shadow filter quality at its default **Low**), which will give you smoother shadows without an increased performance cost.\r\n- Shadow opacity will behave differently to other light types, as the shadow won't fade in an uniform manner across the whole light. This may be desired behavior, but it might be worth documenting to avoid surprises:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cc4cd507-84ef-491c-b1d5-210907fbfc21\r\n\r\n- When you move some shadow casters, they can sometimes be in a position where they will self-shadow. This is most noticeable at low blur values (below `0.3` in the test project). Reloading the scene or restarting the project does *not* fix the self-shadowing, so this does not appear to be an issue related to shadow updates sometimes not occurring when they should.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/131dee5c-c6c1-40d0-bcfc-2d8e68a7dbc\r\n\r\nThe issue will occur even if you're moving another shadow caster:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a254c09-f2ad-47b6-a9ee-9c10f159369e\r\n\r\n- Specular contribution is set to `0.5` by default, which leads to area lights not having specular contributions as strong as omni and spot lights:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8691297e-fd4c-41fa-bdfe-357a1dd5a9cf)\r\n\r\nIt's more in line with other light types when set to `1.0`, so I suggest changing the default to that:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ea361632-ba79-43d9-8a62-61ff05d94eb8)\r\n","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219#pullrequestreview-2983649861","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108219","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-03T15:25:15Z"},{"id":2984685738,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6x5rCq","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219#pullrequestreview-2984685738","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108219","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-03T21:04:28Z"},{"id":3068336882,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc624xry","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"9a38c41538520915c9556233f774f133fe94db9a","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested again, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nNote that in Compatibility, the specular light lobe is missing entirely on both rough and smooth materials. This is not an issue in Forward+ and Mobile.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n>\r\n> When testing the MRP I linked in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219#pullrequestreview-2983649861 on Mobile and Compatibility, keep in mind the per-mesh light limits. The MRP has more than 8 area lights, which means some of them won't appear on the large ground surface until you hide some of them.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219#pullrequestreview-3068336882","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108219","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-29T16:33:49Z"},{"id":3107729813,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc65PDGV","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"2f877a6e8cec58a8b046edc435b636f4e91d907b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48926464?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/LiveTrower","id":48926464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTI2NDY0","login":"LiveTrower","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219#pullrequestreview-3107729813","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108219","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-08-11T20:45:07Z"},{"id":3153338648,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc679CEY","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"2f877a6e8cec58a8b046edc435b636f4e91d907b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53947784?u=1bf2304c9ebf533276295a399e0c7d89c1d9270b&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/CookieBadger","id":53947784,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTQ3Nzg0","login":"CookieBadger","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://a